Sure! Below is an example of HTML, CSS, and Java code for a simple welcoming page. This page includes basic styling and functionality to display a welcome message.

### HTML (index.html)
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Welcome Page</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="welcome-container">
        <h1>Welcome to Our Website!</h1>
        <p>This is a simple welcoming page. You can add more content here to make it more engaging.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

### CSS (styles.css)
```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    margin: 0;
}

.welcome-container {
    background-color: #fff;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    text-align: center;
}

h1 {
    color: #333;
}

p {
    color: #666;
    font-size: 1.2em;
    margin: 10px 0;
}
```

### Java (index.java)
```java
import java.awt.*;
import javax.swing.*;

public class WelcomePage {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        JFrame frame = new JFrame("Welcome Page");
        frame.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);
        frame.setSize(300, 200);
        frame.setLayout(new BorderLayout());

        JPanel welcomePanel = new JPanel();
        welcomePanel.setLayout(new BoxLayout(welcomePanel, BoxLayout.Y_AXIS));

        JLabel welcomeLabel = new JLabel("Welcome to Our Website!");
        welcomeLabel.setFont(new Font("Arial", Font.BOLD, 24));
        welcomeLabel.setHorizontalAlignment(SwingConstants.CENTER);
        welcomePanel.add(welcomeLabel);

        JPanel contentPanel = new JPanel();
        contentPanel.setLayout(new BoxLayout(contentPanel, BoxLayout.Y_AXIS));

        JLabel contentLabel = new JLabel("This is a simple welcoming page. You can add more content here to make it more engaging.");
        contentLabel.setFont(new Font("Arial", Font.BOLD, 16));
        contentPanel.add(contentLabel);

        welcomePanel.add(contentPanel);

        frame.add(welcomePanel, BorderLayout.CENTER);
        frame.setVisible(true);
    }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **HTML**: The HTML file defines the structure of the page, including the welcome message and a button to add more content.
2. **CSS**: The CSS file styles the welcome page, including the container, label, and content. It uses a `BoxLayout` to center the content vertically.
3. **Java**: The Java file creates a simple GUI application that displays the welcome message and a button to add more content. The button is positioned in the center of the welcome panel.

You can run this code in any Java environment to see the welcoming page in action.
